# Docker build context for .devcontainer/dockerfile
#
# WHY THIS IS AN ALLOWLIST
# The build context is the repo root ("context": ".." in devcontainer.json), and
# this repo carries ~12 GB of raw climate data (data/RawData/*.nc is 11.4 GB on
# its own) plus multi-GB runs/ and results/ trees. Without this file Docker ships
# all of it to the daemon on every rebuild, which is slow at best and exhausts
# disk or memory at worst.
#
# The dockerfile only needs ONE file from the context:
#     COPY requirements.txt /tmp/requirements.txt
# so everything is excluded and requirements.txt is added back. Context drops
# from ~12 GB to ~1.5 KB.
#
# IMPORTANT: this affects the BUILD CONTEXT ONLY, not the runtime bind mount.
# data/, runs/, results/ and the rest are still fully visible inside the
# container at /workspaces/Paper_1 -- nothing is hidden from your code.
#
# IF YOU ADD A COPY LINE to the dockerfile, add a matching "!path" exception
# below, otherwise the COPY will silently find nothing.

*
!requirements.txt
